.TH SCRMENU 1A
.SH NAME
scrmenu \- provide description of active screens
.SH SYNOPSIS
scrmenu
.SH DESCRIPTION
scrmenu
provides a description of what programs are running on various
screens.  It allows the user to interactively select
(using the arrow keys), and activate (using the
return key) a screen.  It is intended to be run automatically during
system startup.
.SH SEE ALSO
sioc(1A), screen(7A)
